==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kendo Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''The Kitty of Liberty''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Fencer Cat is good to bring along for [[Cats of the Cosmos]] where you need to destroy that single Barrier. The likes of [[Le'Solar]], [[Youcan]], [[UltraBaaBaa]] and [[Kid Tappa]] can all be made much easier with it gone. Wave Shields should be used in tandem against Youcan, as Fencer does not have [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]].

Fencer Cat is not only good as a Barrier Breaker, though; he can also be used as a decent ranged attacker if boosted, due to his high attack power and lower cooldown than [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]]. This comes at the cost of lower range.

Though his attribute of having just one knockback may seem to hinder him (since ranged attackers usually use knockbacks to escape attacks and reposition), Fencer Cat can tank attacks that would otherwise knock back other ranged attackers and retaliate, in a similar way to [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Kung Fu Cat]]. This does in fact allow him to benefit more from the Barrier Breaker ability, as he will hold position and get the essential hit in, which can easily turn a losing battle in your favor, such as if [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] falters against the formidable Youcan.

==='''True Form'''===
The Kitty of Liberty has greater health, attack power, increased attack rate, and a faster attack animation. These performance improvements do a great deal of help for his main niche, [[Barrier]] [[Barrier Breaker|breaking]]. To start off with the improved health and attack power, they are both pretty minor and about 2k each, nothing too special, other than his DPS jumping from 3.2k to 4.7k. For the attack rate, it was lowered by 30 frames (aka 1 second), this is not that much of an improvement at first glance, but when combined with the faster attack animation, which is by 30 frames for the foreswing and 2 frames for the backswing, it becomes apparent that Fencer Cat gets a lot of improvement out of this [[True Form]].

==='''Talents'''===
The Kitty of Liberty has [[Knockback|knockback]], [[Immune to Warp]], [[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Curse]], and the standard Health and Attack Buffs as their [[talents]]. Knockback is a useless ability, as it pushes targets away from the line of fire. If you wish for a better unit that can knockback Aliens, [[Ancient Egg: N105 (Rare Cat)|Racquet Cat]] is a better unit. [[Immune to Warp]] is also useless, as it denies the unit any chances to reposition through such effects. [[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Curse]] also does nothing, as it's only really useful with Knockback since Curse does not disable Barrier Breaker. Stat buffs are fairly superfluous unless you plan on using him similarly to Kung Fu Cat. Even then, using [[Catseye]]s first is recommended. His single target nature, however, means you're better off investing elsewhere.

==='''Orb'''===
Barriers are exclusive to Alien enemies, so Attack Up vs Aliens will work. Don't use Defense Up vs Aliens because The Kitty of Liberty only has 1 knockback anyway.

For ability orbs, Death Mini-Surge is the only useful one on him, letting Kitty of Liberty to break Barriers post-mortem.

